      "target": "../sections/page-001.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Research article EMH] - Vol. 25 No. 10 - 2019\n\nCost-effectiveness of introducing the pneumococcal conjugate\nvaccine for children under 5 years in the Islamic Republic of Iran\n\nKhadijeh Ezoji’,7, Mohsen Yaghoubi?, Marzieh Nojomi*, Sussan Mahmoody*, Seyed Mohsen Zahraie’, Maziar Moradi-Lakeh*, Sedigheh R. Tabatabaei®\nand Abdollah Karimi®\n\n‘Social Determinants of Health Research Center, Health Research Institute, Babol University of Medical Sciences, Babol, Islamic Republic of Iran. *De-\npartment of Community Medicine, Iran University of Medical Sciences, Tehran, Islamic Republic of Iran. *School",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Opening page of a 2019 Eastern Mediterranean Health Journal article on the cost-effectiveness of introducing the 13-valent pneumococcal conjugate vaccine (PCV-13) for children under 5 in the Islamic Republic of Iran, with authors and affiliations. The abstract describes use of the TRIVAC decision support model to estimate costs and disability-adjusted life years averted for pneumonia, meningitis, otitis media and other pneumococcal disease. The introduction notes that vaccinating young children also reduces disease indirectly by cutting nasopharyngeal carriage.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
