      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 2",
      "pageStart": 2,
      "pageEnd": 2,
      "target": "../sections/page-002.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Research article\n\nEMH] - Vol. 25 No. 10 - 2019\n\nAfterrunning several clinical trials in different regions\nof the world, PCV-10 and PCV-13 have been introduced\nin the national vaccination programmes of more than\n100 countries, including many low- and middle-income\ndeveloping countries. These vaccines have been found to\nbe cost-effective, especially in developing countries with\nlimited health care resources (3,8,9), and can be safely\nadministered at the same time as other vaccines without\ninterference (9).\n\nThe pneumococcal vaccine is not part of the childhood\nimmunization programme in the Islam",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains that PCV-10 and PCV-13 are used in over 100 countries and that pneumococcal vaccine is not in Iran's schedule, although acute respiratory infection was the fourth leading cause of under-5 deaths in 2013. It describes the TRIVAC model, an Excel-based static cohort model developed by LSHTM with PAHO, ProVac and WHO, and the disease states considered. It then outlines the sources used for disease burden and vaccine efficacy inputs.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/10665-385346/blocks/prose-page-003",
